# What must never reach a build context.
#
# `backend/.env` is first on the list and is the one that matters: it holds a
# live OpenAI key, and anything copied into an image stays in that image's
# layers whether or not a later line deletes it. The deployment reads
# `deploy/env.azure` instead — the same settings with the key removed — and
# receives the key itself as a Container Apps secret.

backend/.env
frontend/.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# --- rebuilt inside the image ---
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
backend/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- not needed at run time ---
.git/
.claude/
docs/
runtime/backups/
runtime/logs/
backend/mlruns/
AIS-forecasting-analysis.html
OneDrive_1_08-09-2026.zip
*.zip

# --- the working data, superseded by the bundle ---
# Nothing under runtime/ or data/ is copied directly any more. The image takes
# `deploy/bundle/`, which `scripts/build_scoped_bundle.py` builds: the live run
# and its panel, the order durations cut to the workspace branches, and a
# `sqlite3 .backup` of the database pruned to the same scope (D-137). Keeping
# these out of the context is most of why it fell from 348 MB to 68 MB.
runtime/
data/
deploy/db/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
